<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net10.0;net8.0;net9.0;netstandard2.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
		<RootNamespace>DevOp.Toon</RootNamespace>
		<AssemblyName>DevOp.Toon</AssemblyName>

		<!-- Package Information -->
		<PackageId>DevOp.Toon</PackageId>
		<Version>0.4.0</Version>
		<Authors>Þorvaldur Hafdal</Authors>
		<Company>DevOp</Company>
		<Description>Token-Oriented Object Notation (TOON) - a token-efficient JSON alternative for LLM prompts</Description>
		<PackageTags>toon;format;llm;token;serialization;json</PackageTags>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.md</PackageLicenseFile>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://wiki.devop.is/devop-toon/home</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/vhafdal/DevOp.Toon</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<SignAssembly>true</SignAssembly>
		<AssemblyOriginatorKeyFile>DevOp.snk</AssemblyOriginatorKeyFile>
		<PublicSign>true</PublicSign>
		<Title>DevOp Toon</Title>
		<Copyright>Þorvaldur Hafdal(DevOp)</Copyright>
		<PackageIcon>Assets\DevOp.Toon-128.png</PackageIcon>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>Adds opt-in constant columns for custom 4.4 tables and [ToonExtensionData] support on the legacy profiles, and fixes legacy encoding and typed decoding gaps.
- Adds ToonEncodeOptions.ConstantColumns (default false): with CustomV4_4, a column identical in every row of a table with at least three rows is written once in the header as Name=value, which CustomV4_4 decoding applies to every row; readers from 0.4.0 and earlier cannot decode it; Auto detection now selects CustomV4_4 for an unquoted '=' in a header field list, so such hand-written official input needs an explicit ProtocolVersion
- Breaking: V3_0 and CustomLegacy now write [ToonExtensionData] entries as sibling keys and capture unmatched keys on typed decode, like the 4.x profiles; a key named like the extension property is an ordinary entry, so a 0.4.0 legacy document with the property as a nested object now decodes as a single entry named after the property
- Breaking: keys that name a declared but unbindable member, such as a computed getter-only property, are no longer captured into [ToonExtensionData] on 4.x profiles
- Adds capture of unmatched keys to ToonService.Deserialize&lt;T&gt;(body, "application/json") with numbers as double, while decimal members now receive the exact JSON value; a JSON number beyond the double range, or beyond the decimal range of a decimal member, now throws ToonFormatException instead of yielding an infinity or an OverflowException
- Fixes V3_0 and CustomLegacy encoding: root and declared dictionaries are written as objects, as are types implementing only the generic dictionary interfaces (such as ExpandoObject) on every protocol version; byte arrays inside lists of objects follow ByteArrayFormat; key folding also folds chains below the root; IgnoreNullOrEmpty also omits null, empty and non-finite members of nested objects; scalars in object-typed members of rows are written as columns
- Fixes V3_0 and CustomLegacy typed decoding of structs and of struct dictionary and list members, of int and long members on the path-expansion route, of nested objects in Dictionary&lt;string, object?&gt; targets, of settable members of records outside the constructor, and of list items whose first field is an array, which no longer lose decimal digits; a number outside the range of a numeric member now throws ToonFormatException on every route, including JSON Deserialize, instead of decoding as 0 or an infinity or failing with NotSupportedException, and other tokens in numeric members decode or fail as on 4.x
- Fixes encoding of System.Text.Json JsonNode values (JsonObject, JsonArray, JsonValue), which overflowed the stack; they now encode like their JSON text on every protocol version, at the root and as members, list items and dictionary values, and V3_0 and CustomLegacy no longer write a blank line for a member that IgnoreNullOrEmpty or ExcludeEmptyArrays omits</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>true</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="LICENSE.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="Assets\DevOp.Toon-128.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="Assets\" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<Using Include="DevOp.Toon.Core" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="10.0.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="DevOp.Toon.Core" Version="0.3.0" Condition="'$(Configuration)' != 'Debug' or '$(ToonCoreProjectPath)' == ''" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)' == 'Debug' and '$(ToonCoreProjectPath)' != ''">
		<ProjectReference Include="$(ToonCoreProjectPath)" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup Condition=" '$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0' ">
		<PackageReference Include="System.Collections.Immutable" Version="10.0.2" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<PropertyGroup Condition=" '$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0' ">
		<AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
	</PropertyGroup>


</Project>
